    a: `Some do, but the risk is high. YouTube's policy since 15 July 2025 names mass-produced and repetitive content as inauthentic and not allowed to be monetised. Using AI for scripts, edits and captions is fine. Using generic templates to churn out videos is not. Add your own voice, view and proof.`,
  },
  {
    q: `Do I need a degree or course to become a YouTuber?`,
