  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The scalable-ownership path is to treat the channel as a shop window, not the shop.</strong>
      It scales because you own the price, the customer list and the offer. You can add a course, a cohort, a productised service or a small team without needing a million views. An ad-only channel never gets that.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take: two-stage competition</p>
    <p>
      Ad-led and sponsor-led channels have two hard filters. The first is clearing the Partner Programme bar. The second is staying in front of viewers in a feed you do not control, or winning deals again and again. Many people pass the first and stall at the second. Plan a second income that does not depend on either. Platform rules also move: the Partner Programme bar for new creators is changing in February 2027.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h3>The basic sales layer for each route</h3>

  <p>
    Every route has a payer who has to find and trust you. Learn the basics of selling: say who you help and with what, make a simple offer, show proof, follow up, ask for referrals and have one honest talk about price. Promise no income to yourself or to clients. Collaboration helps too: swapping guest spots with creators in nearby topics and meeting editors and sponsors in creator groups brings the first referrals.
