  <h2 id="ai">AI: leverage and disruption</h2>

  <p>
    AI already helps with research, scripts, captions, translation and rough edits. Two things follow. First, the effort to make an average video falls, so more average videos appear and attention gets harder to win. Second, the value of a real person with real proof goes up.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Start now</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Use AI to outline scripts and clean up captions, and then rewrite in your own voice.</li>
        <li>Test AI editing tools on one video and check what you save in time.</li>
        <li>Keep a list of facts you checked yourself. AI can sound sure and be wrong.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Build toward</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Move to topics where your experience and on-screen proof cannot be generated.</li>
        <li>Build a community: replies, a mailing list or a WhatsApp group you own.</li>
        <li>Offer the AI-assisted work as a service: editing, repurposing and translation for other channels.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The honest read on disruption: templated, faceless and trend-copy channels face the most pressure, from both AI and YouTube's own policy. Channels tied to a real skill and a real person face the least.
  </p>

